    '|a||Pawn to d5 forks the knight and the bishop. The bishop steps back to d7, and the pawn takes the knight: however Black answers, a piece falls.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11720
      voice: gemini:Charon | calm, warm chess coach
    '|a||Which of your pawns can attack two black pieces at once?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4080
      voice: gemini:Charon | calm, warm chess coach
    '|a||Rook to e1 pins the queen to her king. She can only move along the file, and every square there, even taking the rook, loses her for a rook. Here she steps to e7, and the rook takes her with check.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 15560
      voice: gemini:Charon | calm, warm chess coach
    '|a||Look at the e-file: what stands behind Black''s queen?':
      mp3: 
